<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceList> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/SourceOrDestination> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceList> <http://schema.org/domainIncludes> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceList> <http://schema.org/rangeIncludes> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/SourceOrDestination> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceList> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "(Optional) An unordered list of Source elements that provide context about the originating endpoint of a business transfer of which this event is a part."@en .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceList> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceList> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sourceList" .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceList> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" .
# 
# https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestination
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestination> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/SourceOrDestination> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestination> <http://schema.org/domainIncludes> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/SourceOrDestination> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An identifier that denotes the specific source or destination of a business transfer.\nThe semantic role of the identifier is indicated by sourceOrDestinationType. Resolution of that identifier to EU DPP Actor or Facility concepts, when applicable, is handled outside the EPCIS technical carrier layer."@en .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sourceOrDestination" .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestination> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestination> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/jsonldLabel> "destination" .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestination> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/jsonldLabel> "source" .
# 
# https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestinationType
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestinationType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestinationType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/SourceOrDestination> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestinationType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/SDT> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestinationType> <http://schema.org/domainIncludes> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/SourceOrDestination> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestinationType> <http://schema.org/rangeIncludes> <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/SDT> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestinationType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An identifier that indicates the role of SourceOrDestination in a transfer (Owning Party, Possessing Party, or Location).\nThis role determines how the corresponding sourceOrDestination identifier is interpreted. Mapping to EU DPP Actor or Facility concepts, when applicable, is handled outside the EPCIS technical carrier layer."@en .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestinationType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestinationType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sourceOrDestinationType" .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestinationType> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/sourceOrDestinationType> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/jsonldLabel> "type" .
# 
# https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/transformationID
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/transformationID> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/transformationID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/TransformationEvent> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/transformationID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/Transformation> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/transformationID> <http://schema.org/domainIncludes> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/TransformationEvent> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/transformationID> <http://schema.org/rangeIncludes> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/Transformation> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/transformationID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "(Optional) Associates several TransformationEvents with a longer-running Transformation process, therefore linking them together."@en .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/transformationID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/> .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/transformationID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "transformationID" .
<https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/transformationID> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" .
# 
# https://schema.org/address
<https://schema.org/address> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://schema.org/address> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links an Actor or Facility to its postal address, represented as a schema:PostalAddress"@en .
<https://schema.org/address> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://schema.org/address> .
<https://schema.org/address> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has address"@en .
# 
# https://schema.org/geo
<https://schema.org/geo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://schema.org/geo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links facility to its coordinates, represented as schema:geo."@en .
<https://schema.org/geo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://schema.org/geo> .
<https://schema.org/geo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has coordinates"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#accordingTo
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#accordingTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#accordingTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityCertificate> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#accordingTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityAssessmentModule> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#accordingTo> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec/2008/768(1)/oj#art_4\nDecision No 768/2008/EC Art 4"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#accordingTo> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj/#art_43\t\nESPR Art 43"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#accordingTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Property defining specifies conformity assess procedure/cerfication scheme underlying the cerfificate."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#accordingTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "according to"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#addressesAoP
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#addressesAoP> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#addressesAoP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAImpactCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#addressesAoP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#AreaOfProtection> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#addressesAoP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Link between an LCIAImpactCategory and the Area(s)-of-protection it addresses.\n1..n cardinality: a single impact category can address several Areas of Protection — for example, ozone depletion affects both Natural Environment and Human Health."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#addressesAoP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "addresses AoP"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#addressesAoP> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "ILCD base"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#allowsConformityAssessmentModule
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#allowsConformityAssessmentModule> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#allowsConformityAssessmentModule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#UnionHarmonisationLegislation> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#allowsConformityAssessmentModule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityAssessmentModule> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#allowsConformityAssessmentModule> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec/2008/768(1)/oj#art_4\nDecision No 768/2008/EC Art 4"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#allowsConformityAssessmentModule> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj/#art_43\nESPR Art 43"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#allowsConformityAssessmentModule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that specifies the conformity assment procedure applicable to the type of product"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#allowsConformityAssessmentModule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "allows Conformity Assessment Module"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#appliesToProduct
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#appliesToProduct> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#appliesToProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#hasDPP> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#appliesToProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPP> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#appliesToProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Product> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#appliesToProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The property links DPP and the Product."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#appliesToProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "applies to product"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#assessesImpactCategory
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#assessesImpactCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#assessesImpactCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAImpactIndicator> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#assessesImpactCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAImpactCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#assessesImpactCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Link from an LCIA impact indicator to the mid-point impact category it characterises. Multiple indicators may assess the same category (e.g. Eutrophication, freshwater and Eutrophication, marine both relate to Eutrophication). This property expresses a conceptual classification link, not equivalence."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#assessesImpactCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "assesses impact category"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#assessesImpactCategory> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCAnet: relates to the element assessIC (https://w3id.org/lcanet/ia#assessIC) in the IA module."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToEn15804Group
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToEn15804Group> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToEn15804Group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EN15804Indicator> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToEn15804Group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EN15804IndicatorGroup> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToEn15804Group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Link from an EN15804Indicator individual to the indicator EN15804IndicatorGroup it belongs to (core impact, with-caveats, resource use, waste, valorisation, exported energy)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToEn15804Group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "belongs to EN 15804 indicator group"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToEn15804Group> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToMethodology
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToMethodology> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToMethodology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToMethodology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToMethodology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Link from a Method to one or several LCAMethodology individuals it belongs to (e.g. eudpp:methodology_EF3_1). Cardinality 1..n: a single method can be classified into more than one methodology (for example, when two methodologies share the same characterisation factors for one indicator)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToMethodology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "belongs to methodology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToMethodology> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#belongsToMethodology> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCAnet: relates to the element includedInMethodology (https://w3id.org/lcanet/ia#includedInMethodology) in the IA module." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#computedByMethod
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#computedByMethod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#computedByMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAIndicator> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#computedByMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#computedByMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Link from an LCAIndicator individual to the IndicatorMethod instance that describes how this indicator is computed — its impact model, impact category, methodology reference, reference report, and ILCD method metadata. \nCardinality: at most 1 per indicator individual.\""@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#computedByMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "computed by method"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#computedByMethod> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsDPP
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsDPP> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsDPP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPPEvent> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsDPP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPP> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsDPP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a DPP event to the Digital Product Passport whose content, state, or accessibility is affected by the event. This is a cross-module relation between EVENT and P_DPP and is therefore managed in the Connector/mapping layer.\n\nDPP is modelled in the EU DPP CO P_DPP module.\nDPPEvent is modelled in the EU DPP CO EVENT module."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsDPP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "concerns DPP"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsProduct
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsProduct> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ProductEvent> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Product> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a product event to the product whose state, condition, or lifecycle is affected by the event. This is a cross-module relation between EVENT and P_DPP and is therefore managed in the Connector/mapping layer.\n\nProduct is modelled in the EU DPP CO P_DPP module.\nProductEvent is modelled in the EU DPP CO EVENT module."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "concerns product"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsSubstance
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsSubstance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsSubstance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstancePresence> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsSubstance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstanceOfConcern> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsSubstance> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Article 7(5)(a)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsSubstance> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsSubstance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a reported SubstancePresence to the SubstanceOfConcern involved. dpp:Substance remains the superclass used for generic substance identity and naming properties, but the SOC reporting relation itself is intentionally restricted to dpp:SubstanceOfConcern."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsSubstance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/SOC> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsSubstance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Concerns substance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#concernsSubstance> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceStatus> "ESPR-grounded ontology modelling abstraction; this RDF resource is not itself a term defined by the Regulation."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAttestedBy
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAttestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAttestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#UnionHarmonisationLegislation> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAttestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Actor> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAttestedBy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Annex V (7)" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAttestedBy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj/#anx_%C2%A0V" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAttestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Specifies the notified body that attest the product's conformity with Union harmonisation legislation. \n\nUnionHarmonisationLegislation is modelled in the EU DPP CO COMP module.\nActor is modelled in the EU DPP CO ACTOR module."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAttestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "conformity attested by"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityDeclaredTo
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityDeclaredTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityDeclaredTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EUDeclarationOfConformity> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityDeclaredTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#UnionHarmonisationLegislation> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityDeclaredTo> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ESPR Annex V"@en .
