# https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAResult> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid98 .
_:genid98 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EN15804InventoryIndicator> .
_:genid98 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger> .
_:genid98 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#quantifiesIndicator> .
_:genid98 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A specific LCA result representing an aggregated inventory-indicator result computed for an EN 15804+A2 inventory indicator (Table 5: resource use, waste categories, output flows). \nImportant disambiguation: this class represents the AGGREGATED inventory-indicator value (e.g. total kg of HWD across A1-A3 for one product), as printed in EN 15804+A2 EPD tables and computed by a Method instance. It is NOT the raw flow-level life-cycle inventory (LCI) result of a process (which would be a list of elementary-flow exchanges with amounts and units, and is out of scope for this DPP-oriented LCA module)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Inventory Indicator Result"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "ILCD+EPD extension"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAIndicator
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid99 .
_:genid99 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod> .
_:genid99 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger> .
_:genid99 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#computedByMethod> .
_:genid99 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Abstract umbrella class for an indicator definition (impact or inventory category) that an eudpp:Method calculates values for. \nEach instance identifies exactly one method under which it is computed; this constraint is formalised as owl:maxCardinality 1 on eudpp:computedByMethod. \nNote: an indicator individual is the indicator DEFINITION (e.g. \"FW – Net use of fresh water, in m3\"); a numerical value computed for that indicator on a specific study is an eudpp:LCAResult instance (LCIAResult or InventoryIndicatorResult)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LCA Indicator"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAIndicator> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A life-cycle assessement method that produces values for one indicator from an inventory of elementary flows. \nCovers both (a) characterised LCIA methods (which apply characterisation factors to compute a midpoint impact result), and (b) inventory aggregation methods (which sum / aggregate inventory flows to produce an inventory-indicator result, e.g. the EN 15804+A2 inventory indicators FW, HWD, PERE etc. defined as inventory-level by the standard's calculation rules)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LCA Method"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://indatawg.github.io/ILCD-EPD-Data-Format/gitBranches/release/v1.3/schemadoc/ILCD_LCIAMethodDataSet.html> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "ILCD+EPD extension: corresponds to the element LCIA Method Data Set, which is used in practice for both LCIA method and inventory indicator methods."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCAnet: relates to the element Method (https://w3id.org/lcanet/ia#Method) in the IA module."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodReport
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodReport> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodReport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Source> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodReport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Source that documents a life-cycle impact assessment (LCIA) method (e.g. the EF 3.1 method description)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodReport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LCIA Method Report"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodReport> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broadMatch> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodReport> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "ILCD base"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named, versioned LCA methodology (a coherent set of LCA methods sharing principles and a set of characterisation factors), to which one or more Method instances belong. \nEach individual SHOULD carry a skos:altLabel giving a short code (e.g. \"EF 3.1\") and eudpp:methodologyVersion giving the version identifier."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LCA Methodology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCAnet: relates to the element Methodology (https://w3id.org/lcanet/ia#Methodology) of the IA module."@en .
# 
