<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Abstract class for any LCA computation output of a study. Has three subclasses: \neudpp:LCIAResult (characterised impact result) which applies characterisation factors of an LCIA method, eudpp:InventoryIndicatorResult (aggregated inventory-indicator result) whcih is a sum/aggregation over the inventory without characterisation, and eudpp:EnvironmentalFootprintScoreResult which represents the aggregated EF single score result. \n\nIn the regulatory sense of ESPR Art. 2(24), some characterized individuals of LCAResult constitute environmental footprints — quantifications of environmental impacts of a product throughout its life cycle.Other LCAResult instances, however, fall outside the strict ESPR definition. For this reason, LCAResult is linked to the ESPR \"Environmental Footprint\" concept via skos:broadMatch rather than owl:equivalentClass."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LCA Result"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAResult> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broadMatch> "ESPR Art 2 (24) https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj#Art2_24"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAResult> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAResult> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCAnet: relates to the element LcaResult (https://w3id.org/lcanet/ia#LcaResult) of the IA module."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAStudy
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAStudy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAStudy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A life-cycle assessment study of a product, conducted per ISO 14040/14044, producing one or more LCA results. The general study container, applicable to any product whether or not the study follows EN 15804+A2. \nCarries study-level metadata (UUID, dataset version, name, reference year, license, copyright, ILCD format version, compliance declarations, manufacturer records, reviews, references to data sources / background databases / PEFCR, etc.). \nCross-module link from a product to this class is provided by the Connector property eudpp:hasLCAStudy."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAStudy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAStudy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LCA Study"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAStudy> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAStudy> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCAnet: relates to the element LcaModel (https://w3id.org/lcanet/core#LcaModel) of the Core module, which represents an LCA instance."@en .
