# https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstanceIdentifierScheme> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#identifierExampleValue> "200-578-6" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#identifierMaxLength> "9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#identifierPattern> "^[2-5]\\d{2}-\\d{3}-\\d$" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "EC number is a unique identification number assigned to a chemical substance in the European Union. It is used to identify substances in regulatory databases, safety data sheets (SDSs), and chemical legislation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The EC number is a seven-digit identifier typically written in the format XXX-XXX-X and used to identify chemical substances in European regulatory inventories.\n\nExample:\nSubstance: Ethanol\nEC number: 200-578-6"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EC"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#ECHA
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ECHA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ECHA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstanceIdentifierScheme> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ECHA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "ECHA substance identification scheme refers to the approach used by the European Chemicals Agency (ECHA) to identify and distinguish chemical substances for regulatory purposes under EU chemicals legislation, particularly REACH."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ECHA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ECHA"@en .
