# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAssessmentBody
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAssessmentBody> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAssessmentBody> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityAssessmentRole> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAssessmentBody> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Art 2 (52)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAssessmentBody> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAssessmentBody> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Conformity assessment body means a body that performs conformity assessment activities including calibration, testing, certification and inspection; [ESPR Art 2 (52)]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#conformityAssessmentBody> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Conformity Assessment Body"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#consumer
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#consumer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#consumer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EndUserRole> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#consumer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#customer> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#consumer> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "Directive (EU) 2019/771, Art 2 (2)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#consumer> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2019/771/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#consumer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Consumer means any natural person who, in relation to contracts covered by Directive (EU) 2019/771, is acting for purposes which are outside that person's trade, business, craft or profession; [Directive (EU) 2019/771, Art 2 (2)]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#consumer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Consumer"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#credentialAgency
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#credentialAgency> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#credentialAgency> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Role> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#credentialAgency> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "CIRPASS-2 User Stories 3.1"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#credentialAgency> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://zenodo.org/records/17979585" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#credentialAgency> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A legal person that provides (professional) credentials to parties, which may be used to make and verify a variety of claims in the DPP, (ESPR) Art. 11 last paragraph. For example, a credentials agency could certify a professional repairer and provide appropriate credentials for the DPP system; [CIRPASS-2 User Stories 3.1]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#credentialAgency> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Credential Agency"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#customer
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EndUserRole> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customer> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Art 2 (35)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customer> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Customer means a natural or legal person that purchases, hires or receives a product for their own use whether or not acting for purposes which are outside their trade, business, craft or profession; [ESPR Art 2 (35)]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Customer"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#customsAuthority
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customsAuthority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customsAuthority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#AuthorityRole> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customsAuthority> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, Art 3 (24)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customsAuthority> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2019/1020/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customsAuthority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Customs authorities means  customs authorities as defined in point 1 of Article 5 of Regulation (EU) No 952/2013; [Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, Art 3 (24)]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customsAuthority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Customs authorities means the customs administrations of the Member States responsible for applying the customs legislation and any other authorities empowered under national law to apply certain customs legislation (Regulation (EU) No 952/2013 Art 5 (1);"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#customsAuthority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Customs Authority"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#dealer
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dealer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dealer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EconomicOperatorRole> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dealer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#distributor> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dealer> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Art 2 (55)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dealer> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dealer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Dealer means a distributor or any other natural or legal person that offers products for sale, hire or hire purchase, or that displays products, to end users in the course of a commercial activity, including through distance selling; and includes any natural or legal person that puts a product into service in the course of a commercial activity; [ESPR Art 2 (55)]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dealer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dealer"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#dependentInternalReview
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dependentInternalReview> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dependentInternalReview> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#TypeOfReview> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dependentInternalReview> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reviewer involved in data collection or modelling, or representing the process/product system. Not acceptable for EN 15804+A2 compliance."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dependentInternalReview> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dependent internal review"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dependentInternalReview> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "ILCD base" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#distributor
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#distributor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#distributor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EconomicOperatorRole> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#distributor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#dealer> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#distributor> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Art 2 (45)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#distributor> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#distributor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Distributor means any natural or legal person in the supply chain, other than the manufacturer or the importer, that makes a product available on the market; [ESPR Art 2 (45)]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#distributor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Distributor"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#dppServiceProvider
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dppServiceProvider> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dppServiceProvider> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Role> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dppServiceProvider> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Art 2 (32)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dppServiceProvider> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dppServiceProvider> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Digital product passport service provider means a natural or legal person that is an independent third-party authorised by the economic operator which places the product on the market or puts it into service and that processes the digital product passport data for that product for the purpose of making such data available to economic operators and other relevant actors with a right to access those data under this Regulation or other Union law; [ESPR Art 2 (32)]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#dppServiceProvider> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "DPP Service Provider"@en .
