<https://w3id.org/eudpp#massFractionUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#massFractionUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://si-digital-framework.org/SI#MeasurementUnit> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#massFractionUnit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "SI style convention: percent denotes the number 0.01; mass fraction values should be represented as decimal ratios in data."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#massFractionUnit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://physics.nist.gov/cuu/Units/checklist.html> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#massFractionUnit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://si-digital-framework.org/> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#massFractionUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Project-managed measurement-unit convention for dimensionless mass fraction expressed as a decimal ratio of masses. Use dpp:numericalValue \"0.001\"^^xsd:decimal for 0.1 % by mass. This avoids encoding \"w/w\" in the unit symbol and may be replaced by an official SI Digital Framework PID if one becomes available."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#massFractionUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/SOC> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#massFractionUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mass fraction unit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#massFractionUnit> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceStatus> "Implementation measurement-unit convention; not a named SI Digital Framework unit PID."@en .
